<body>
    <h1>User Guide</h1>
    <p><strong>Application Name:</strong> MARK Operating System<br>
    <strong>Version:</strong> 1.0.0<br>
    <strong>Last Updated:</strong> 2025</p>

    <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#getting-started">Getting Started</a></li>
        <li><a href="#core-features">Core Features</a></li>
        <li><a href="#usage-workflows">Usage Workflows</a></li>
        <li><a href="#configuration">Configuration</a></li>
        <li><a href="#best-practices">Best Practices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#support">Support & Resources</a></li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="overview">1. Overview</h2>
    <p>MARK is an intelligent operating system designed to coordinate specialist AI workers for complex engineering tasks. It provides a structured framework for task decomposition, worker orchestration, and result aggregation.</p>

    <h3>Key Concepts</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>MARK (Master Agent for Recursive Knowledge):</strong> The central orchestration layer</li>
        <li><strong>Workers:</strong> Specialized AI agents (Engineer, Planner, Researcher, QA, etc.)</li>
        <li><strong>Milestones:</strong> Discrete units of work assigned to workers</li>
        <li><strong>Tools:</strong> Capabilities available to workers (file ops, terminal, search, git)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="note">
        <strong>Note:</strong> This guide assumes you have completed the initial setup. See <a href="setup_instructions.docx">Setup Instructions</a> for installation details.
    </div>

    <h2 id="getting-started">2. Getting Started</h2>

    <h3>2.1 Prerequisites</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Python 3.10+</li>
        <li>Git</li>
        <li>Access to LLM API (OpenAI, Anthropic, or local)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.2 First Run</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Clone the repository</li>
        <li>Install dependencies: <code>pip install -r requirements.txt</code></li>
        <li>Configure environment variables (see Configuration section)</li>
        <li>Run: <code>python -m mark</code></li>
    </ol>

    <h3>2.3 Basic Interaction</h3>
    <p>MARK operates through a milestone-based system. You define a milestone, MARK plans the work, assigns workers, and delivers results.</p>

    <pre><code># Example milestone submission
mark submit --milestone "Build user authentication API"
</code></pre>

    <h2 id="core-features">3. Core Features</h2>

    <h3>3.1 Worker Types</h3>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Worker</th><th>Role</th><th>Tools</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Engineer</td><td>Write, edit, structure code</td><td>File ops, Terminal, Git, Search</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Planner</td><td>Decompose tasks, create plans</td><td>File ops, Search</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Researcher</td><td>Gather information, analyze</td><td>Search, Web fetch, File ops</td></tr>
            <tr><td>QA</td><td>Test, validate, review</td><td>Terminal, File ops, Search</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Documenter</td><td>Create docs, guides</td><td>File ops, Search</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>3.2 Tool System</h3>
    <p>Workers have access to a defined toolset:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><code>read_file</code> - Read any file in workspace</li>
        <li><code>write_file</code> - Create or overwrite files</li>
        <li><code>list_directory</code> - Explore project structure</li>
        <li><code>search_workspace</code> - Grep through files</li>
        <li><code>run_terminal</code> - Execute shell commands</li>
        <li><code>git_status</code> / <code>git_diff</code> / <code>git_commit</code> - Git operations</li>
        <li><code>rename_file</code> / <code>delete_file</code> - File management</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>3.3 Milestone Lifecycle</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Submit:</strong> User submits milestone with requirements</li>
        <li><strong>Plan:</strong> Planner breaks down into sub-tasks</li>
        <li><strong>Assign:</strong> MARK assigns workers to sub-tasks</li>
        <li><strong>Execute:</strong> Workers complete assigned work</li>
        <li><strong>Review:</strong> QA validates results</li>
        <li><strong>Deliver:</strong> Results presented to user</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="usage-workflows">4. Usage Workflows</h2>

    <h3>4.1 Code Development Workflow</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Submit milestone: "Implement user registration endpoint"</li>
        <li>Planner creates specification</li>
        <li>Engineer writes implementation</li>
        <li>QA writes and runs tests</li>
        <li>Documenter updates API docs</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>4.2 Debugging Workflow</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Submit milestone: "Fix memory leak in data processor"</li>
        <li>Researcher analyzes codebase for patterns</li>
        <li>Engineer implements fix</li>
        <li>QA runs regression tests</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>4.3 Refactoring Workflow</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Submit milestone: "Refactor authentication module"</li>
        <li>Planner identifies affected components</li>
        <li>Engineer performs refactoring incrementally</li>
        <li>QA validates behavior preservation</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="configuration">5. Configuration</h2>

    <h3>5.1 Environment Variables</h3>
    <pre><code># Required
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
# or
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here

# Optional
MARK_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
MARK_WORKSPACE_PATH=/path/to/workspace
MARK_MAX_WORKERS=5
MARK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
</code></pre>

    <h3>5.2 Worker Configuration</h3>
    <p>Worker behavior can be customized via <code>config/workers.yaml</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>engineer:
  model: gpt-4
  temperature: 0.2
  max_tokens: 4000

planner:
  model: gpt-4
  temperature: 0.3
</code></pre>

    <h3>5.3 Tool Permissions</h3>
    <p>Each worker has a defined tool permission scope. Modify in <code>config/permissions.yaml</code>.</p>

    <h2 id="best-practices">6. Best Practices</h2>

    <h3>6.1 Writing Effective Milestones</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Be specific about desired outcomes</li>
        <li>Include acceptance criteria</li>
        <li>Reference existing code/files when relevant</li>
        <li>Specify constraints (performance, compatibility, etc.)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>6.2 Monitoring Progress</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Check MARK logs for worker activity</li>
        <li>Review git commits for incremental changes</li>
        <li>Use <code>mark status</code> to see current milestone state</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>6.3 Iterative Development</h3>
    <p>Break large features into smaller milestones for better control and review checkpoints.</p>

    <div class="warning">
        <strong>Warning:</strong> Avoid submitting milestones that modify the same files concurrently. This can cause conflicts.
    </div>

    <h2 id="support">7. Support & Resources</h2>

    <h3>7.1 Documentation</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="setup_instructions.docx">Setup Instructions</a></li>
        <li><a href="troubleshooting_guide.docx">Troubleshooting Guide</a></li>
        <li>Architecture docs in <code>docs/canonical/</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>7.2 Common Commands</h3>
    <pre><code>mark submit "milestone description"    # Submit new milestone
mark status                            # Check current status
mark logs                              # View worker logs
mark workers                           # List available workers
mark config                            # Show current configuration
</code></pre>

    <h3>7.3 Getting Help</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Check troubleshooting guide for common issues</li>
        <li>Review worker logs for error details</li>
        <li>Consult architecture documentation for system understanding</li>
    </ul>

    <hr>
    <p><em>End of User Guide</em></p>
